What is an Aero-Engine?
An aero-engine or aircraft engine is the component of the propulsion system for an aircraft that generates mechanical power. Aircraft engines are almost always either lightweight piston engines or gas turbines, except for small multi copter UAVs which are almost always electric aircraft.
The Aero-engine industry is highly concentrated, with only a few manufacturers worldwide. High-end products mainly come from North America and Europe. Market competition is relatively intense, with GE, Pratt & Whitney, Rolls-Royce and Safran leading the industry, holding about 97% market shares.
